            "When King Darius signed a law that no one could pray to any god but the king for thirty days, Daniel went home, climbed to his upper room where the windows were open toward Jerusalem, and knelt three times a day, “as he had done previously” (Daniel 6:10). Notice those words. Daniel did not invent a new spiritual life when the crisis came. He simply kept the one he already had.",
